description:
Design a synchronous 4-bit binary counter with a reset function. When the reset (RST) input is low, the counter output (Q) is set to zero. On each positive edge of the clock, if reset is not asserted, the counter increments its value by one, utilizing a series of registers (Q1, Q2, Q3, Q4) to hold intermediate values and ensure stable output. The design captures a sequential counting behavior, suitable for applications requiring a binary count sequence.
module top_module(
    input clk,      // Added clk input
    input RST,
    output reg [3:0] Q
);

code:
module top_module(
    input clk,      // Added clk input
    input RST,
    output reg [3:0] Q
);reg [3:0] Q1, Q2, Q3, Q4;

always @(posedge clk) begin
    Q1 <= Q;
    Q2 <= Q1;
    Q3 <= Q2;
    Q4 <= Q3;
    if (RST == 0) begin
        Q <= 4'b0000;
    end else begin
        Q <= Q4 + 1;
    end
end

endmodule

