description:
Design a clock divider that counts the number of clock cycles. On each rising edge of the input clock, it increments a 32-bit register `clkdiv`. When the reset signal is asserted, it sets `clkdiv` to zero, effectively allowing for a reset of the counter. This module can be used to generate a slower clock signal or to create a timing reference in digital systems, based on the input clock.
module top_module(
	input wire clk, rst, 
	output reg [31:0] clkdiv
    );

code:
module top_module(
	input wire clk, rst, 
	output reg [31:0] clkdiv
    );always @ (posedge clk or posedge rst) begin
		if (rst) clkdiv <= 0;
		else clkdiv <= clkdiv + 1'b1;
	end
endmodule

